    "b-ks2-path-sync-intro": {
      "id": "b-ks2-path-sync-intro",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "SYNC — The between-runs phase: material flowing in from outside the run loop. Three pathways carry it — pull requests, Discord exports, wiki mirror syncs — each fired by its importer landing new source rows. kg2-ingest runs its lanes in a fixed order — reconcile first (rename continuity at the new checkout head), then prs, then discord, then attempts. The wiki lane is opt-in: it is in neither the default sync set nor all and fires only on an explicit --lane wiki, because the mirror rarely changes and its import is slow. Every importer writes source rows only, advances its "
        },
        {
          "insert": "source_watermark",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " row, and enqueues index tasks: the PR importer enqueues "
        },
        {
          "insert": "pr_imported",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", and the Discord and wiki importers both enqueue "
        },
        {
          "insert": "archival_ingest",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " tasks whose payload names the source. Boundary sync's hand-off to kg2-ingest is still a manual step. Nothing here waits on a run boundary."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
